      "counterfactual": "If the boundary had been fully released and all changes documented, this specific gap between preparation state and distribution compliance would not exist.",
      "competingExplanation": "The interruption could have occurred without any change to arrangements; however, the lack of documentation (n-18qtamm) remains a condition that permits such an unrecorded scenario if one existed.","evidenceGap":"No evidence confirms whether a service-routing change actually occurred or was implemented prior to the incident. The blank attachment field does not prove absence of changes, only absence of record for them at issue time (n-109kb97)."}
    ],
    "decision": {
      "summary": "The investigation identifies that while a service-routing change may have occurred without proper documentation (hypothesis), the evidence currently supports only procedural gaps: draft preparation did not satisfy distribution requirements, and no temporary instruction was attached. The causal chain remains incomplete because there is no confirmed unrecorded routing change or valve state alteration to link directly to the air interruption.",
      "evidenceUsed": ["0ff450fe-49da-4c67-8b42-35449fdad35c#1", "eaee59fe-70f4-4876-a21d-780814412078#1"],
      "unknowns": ["Whether a service-routing change occurred or was implemented before the incident.", "The exact point of interruption (source, distribution system, receiving equipment).", "Valve states at the time of the event."],
      "alternatives": [
        "An external factor (third-party work, utility outage) caused the interruption without any internal procedural failure.",
        "A documented change was properly executed but not recorded in available evidence due to sampling limitations or record retention policies."
      ],
      "confidence": 0.65
